      "biography": {
        "value": "<p><em>Waluipedia cast sheet — Mario.</em> Built by <code>tools/build-character-sheets.py</code>, hand-authored from the article. XP ledger: level 5, power rating 14 → a level 5 Monk player-character sheet (a player may take this seat; the authored CR 5 stands in where the ledger is silent). Numbers are a GM-ready reading of the record, not a filed stat line; the article stays the authority. Archive date 1040 BF.</p><p><strong>The Plumber Who Vanished</strong> — Mushroom Kingdom (Former Hero) / Unknown</p><p>Status: Missing — Presumed alive, location unknown, last confirmed sighting 1039 BF at the Star Fountain</p><p>Mario is—or WAS—the most famous hero in the Mushroom Kingdom. The man who saved Princess Peach countless times before her assassination in 955 BF. The red-capped plumber who could jump higher than physics should allow, who stomped Bowser's schemes into the ground repeatedly, who was so synonymous with heroism that his NAME became a verb. And then, after eighty-five years of diminished appearances and growing silence, he DISAPPEARED entirely. Luigi found him at the Star Fountain. They flew together on wing caps. Luigi said 'Nothing can hurt us... as long as we're together.' And then Mario was GONE again, and Luigi is working alone for the Mages' Guild at Raventree Manor, sucking up ghosts with a vacuum cleaner and refusing to explain ANYTHING. Waluigi has spent considerable effort piecing together what happened. The picture that emerges is worse than a simple disappearance. WAH. The Garden Above the Fire does not return Mario; it makes his absence louder, because Luigi's rescue ends with Luigi asking the brother who is not in the room whether they are still superstars.</p><h3>Evidence</h3><ul><li><strong>Stomp</strong> — “The red-capped plumber who could jump higher than physics should allow, who stomped Bowser's schemes into the ground repeatedly, who was so synonymous with heroism that his NAME became a verb.”</li><li><strong>Prodigious Leap</strong> — “The red-capped plumber who could jump higher than physics should allow, who stomped Bowser's schemes into the ground repeatedly, who was so synonymous with heroism that his NAME became a verb.”</li><li><strong>Extra Attack</strong> — “The red-capped plumber who could jump higher than physics should allow, who stomped Bowser's schemes into the ground repeatedly, who was so synonymous with heroism that his NAME became a verb.”</li><li><strong>Wing Cap (1/Day)</strong> — “They flew together on wing caps.”</li><li><strong>Diminished</strong> — “And then, after eighty-five years of diminished appearances and growing silence, he DISAPPEARED entirely.”</li><li><strong>Missing Since 1039 BF</strong> — “Missing — Presumed alive, location unknown, last confirmed sighting 1039 BF at the Star Fountain”</li></ul><p>Article: <code>#/article/mario</code> (characters). Site sheet: <code>#/sheets/mario</code>.</p>",
        "public": ""
      }
